kilix-needle (0.20261116+packaging8) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Offer a wording the command grammar reads when Ask plans nothing. Off
    by default; "kilix-needle workflows suggest --set model" takes it from
    the selected command model's own proposal and "--set NAME" from a
    decision model on the local Ollama server, which must agree with the
    command model when one is selected. KILIX_ASK_SUGGEST overrides the
    saved setting. The wording is shown as a hint and never run.
  * A decision model builds the suggested wording from the continuations
    the grammar allows and must pick the same sentence when it ranks the
    complete ones. This asks fewer than half the questions of asking for
    each operation and argument in turn.
  * Read a message or task wholly inside single or typographic quotes
    without the quote marks: "tell claude: 'fix it'" sent the quotes.
  * Read many more ways of saying a supported Ask request, with no model:
    other openers ("kick off", "spin up", "get ... going", "pop open"),
    a bare directory name after "in", ./ and ../ paths, splits and waits
    said many ways, quoted messages introduced by "say", "relay", "ping",
    "let ... know", lists of applications, "it" and "there" for the step
    before, and steps listed as "first ..., second ..." or "1) ... 2) ...".
    A message or task read this way must be quoted, and the whole request
    must also pass the rules suggestions are held to. See
    docs/ask-phrasing.md.
  * Let Ask wait for or message a session named by its Kilix pane ("tell
    pane 143: ...", "the Codex session in pane 9", "pane 32 on broker
    <id>"). Before anything is typed the pane must exist, have the broker
    the request names, and hold a live coding-agent session of the named
    agent in a state that takes the message; a shell, an editor or a tmux
    client is refused. The tool schema the command models use is
    unchanged, and their proposals cannot carry a pane. See
    docs/ask-pane-targets.md.

